======================  CRASH-CAUSING MISTAKES — DO NOT DO THESE  ======================
Past attempts threw errors and scored zero because of API misuse. Follow these rules exactly:
- The object `brush` already exists as a global; do NOT write `const brush = ...`,
  do NOT write `Brush` (capital B), do NOT call `new Brush()`, do NOT import anything.
- There is NO brush.reset() function. Never call it. To change state just call
  brush.set(...), brush.fill(...), brush.noFill(), brush.noField() again with new values.
- brushName must be spelled EXACTLY as one of these strings (case-sensitive, no abbreviations):
  'pen'  'rotring'  '2B'  'HB'  '2H'  'cpencil'  'pastel'  'crayon'  'charcoal'  'spray'  'marker'
  Do NOT write 'cpen', 'pencil', 'ink', or any other variant — those throw.
- field name must be spelled EXACTLY as one of: 'hand' 'curved' 'zigzag' 'waves' 'seabed' 'spiral' 'columns'.
  Pick only ONE per brush.field() call.
- Only call methods that appear in the API list below. Never call brush.reset, brush.background,
  brush.stroke, brush.color, or any p5 built-in like fill()/stroke()/circle() directly — those
  are NOT part of this API and either don't exist or will conflict with p5.brush's own state.
- Wrap the whole body of paint() in a try/catch is NOT required, but every brush.* call you
  write must use a real method name and real argument types (numbers, arrays of [x,y] pairs,
  or the exact string constants above). A single typo throws and the whole sketch scores zero.
- Before submitting, re-read every brush.set(...) and brush.field(...) call and verify the
  string argument is copied verbatim from the allowed lists above.

