The judge checks five things: (1) two equal-radius wheels on one ground line, (2) one closed
frame polygon touching both hubs, (3) a fork line from the head tube straight into the front
hub plus a handlebar, (4) a chainring linked by two chain lines to the rear hub, (5) it
reads as a painted bicycle (visible colour washes plus ink linework), not a bare outline.
