  const FH = [ 120, 90];   // front hub
  const BB = [ -40, 90];   // bottom bracket
  const ST = [ -90, -60];  // top of seat tube
  const HT = [  95, -40];  // head tube top
  const HB = [  60, -90];  // handlebar grip

  // ---- 0. WASH (paint first, behind everything) ----
  brush.fill(WASH_A, 90);
  brush.fillBleed(0.15, 'out');
  brush.fillTexture(0.6, 0.4);
  brush.polygon([[RH[0]-R, -20], [FH[0]+R, -20], [FH[0]+R, 160], [RH[0]-R, 160]]);
  brush.noFill();

  // ---- 1. WHEELS (equal radius, perfectly circular — do not touch these lines) ----
  brush.noField();
  brush.set('rotring', INK_COLOUR, 2);
  brush.circle(RH[0], RH[1], R, false);
  brush.circle(FH[0], FH[1], R, false);
  brush.circle(RH[0], RH[1], 6, false);
  brush.circle(FH[0], FH[1], 6, false);
  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    const a = i * (TWO_PI / 4);
    brush.line(RH[0], RH[1], RH[0] + R * cos(a), RH[1] + R * sin(a));
    brush.line(FH[0], FH[1], FH[0] + R * cos(a), FH[1] + R * sin(a));
  }

  // ---- 2. CLOSED FRAME (one continuous closed polygon — do not touch these vertices) ----
  brush.set('pen', INK_COLOUR, 3);
  brush.polygon([RH, BB, HT, ST, RH]);

  // ---- 3. FORK + STEERING (must touch FH and HT exactly — do not touch these coords) ----
  brush.line(HT[0], HT[1], FH[0], FH[1]);
  brush.line(HT[0], HT[1], HB[0], HB[1]);
  brush.line(HB[0] - 15, HB[1] - 8, HB[0] + 15, HB[1] + 8);

  // ---- 4. DRIVETRAIN (chainring at BB, chain to RH — do not touch these coords) ----
  brush.circle(BB[0], BB[1], 24, false);
  brush.line(BB[0] + 22, BB[1] - 4, RH[0] + 18, RH[1] - 4);
  brush.line(BB[0] + 22, BB[1] + 4, RH[0] + 18, RH[1] + 4);
  brush.line(BB[0], BB[1], BB[0] + 18, BB[1] + 18);

  // ---- 5. SEAT + extra decoration (free to customise) ----
  brush.set('2B', INK_COLOUR, 2);
  brush.wiggle(0.15);
  brush.line(ST[0] - 12, ST[1] - 6, ST[0] + 12, ST[1] - 6);
  brush.wiggle(0);

  brush.fill(WASH_B, 70);
  brush.circle(BB[0], BB[1], 30, false);
  brush.noFill();
}

======================  WHY PAST ATTEMPTS FAILED  ======================
(a) One sketch referenced P5Brush (undeclared global) and crashed instantly — scored zero.
    Never reference anything but `brush`, const/let you declared, JS keywords, or the p5
    builtins listed above.
(b) Other sketches rewrote the wheel/frame/fork/chain coordinates from scratch instead of
    copying the skeleton, producing unequal wheels, an open frame, a disconnected fork, or
    a missing chain — each of those is a separate checklist item and each miss costs real
    points. The skeleton above already satisfies all five checklist items; changing its
    numbers is the single most common cause of failure. When in doubt, copy the skeleton
    verbatim and only touch section 0 (wash), section 5 (seat/decoration), and colour/brush
    names — that is the safest path to a perfect score.

======================  WHAT YOU MAY CHANGE  ======================
- INK_COLOUR, WASH_A, WASH_B hex values (pick saturated, non-white colours).
- brush.fill opacity (60-120), brush.fillBleed/fillTexture numbers.
- brush names used in brush.set (must be one of: 'pen' 'rotring' '2B' 'HB' '2H' 'cpencil'
  'pastel' 'crayon' 'charcoal' 'spray' 'marker').
- Adding extra decorative brush.spline/brush.hatch/brush.wiggle calls, as long as you never
  wiggle or field-warp the wheel circles, hub points, or chainring circle, and never delete
  or renumber sections 1-4.
- Adding a saddle shape, extra washes, extra spokes, hatching for shading.

Do NOT call brush.noWiggle, brush.noStroke, brush.background, brush.reset, brush.stroke,
brush.color, or any method not in this list: brush.set, brush.line, brush.spline,
brush.circle, brush.polygon, brush.beginShape, brush.vertex, brush.endShape, brush.fill,
brush.fillBleed, brush.fillTexture, brush.noFill, brush.hatchStyle, brush.hatch,
brush.noHatch, brush.field, brush.noField, brush.wiggle. Field name (if used) must be
exactly one of: 'hand' 'curved' 'zigzag' 'waves' 'seabed' 'spiral' 'columns', and never
active while drawing the wheel circles, hubs, or chainring.

======================  FINAL CHECK BEFORE YOU EMIT  ======================
1. Does the function contain brush.circle(RH[0], RH[1], R, false) and
   brush.circle(FH[0], FH[1], R, false) with the SAME R — equal wheels?
2. Does it contain brush.polygon([RH, BB, HT, ST, RH]) unchanged — closed frame?
3. Does it contain brush.line(HT[0], HT[1], FH[0], FH[1]) unchanged — fork touching FH?
4. Does it contain brush.circle(BB[0], BB[1], 24, false) plus the two chain
   brush.line calls to RH — drivetrain?
5. Is every colour identifier declared as a const earlier in this SAME function, spelled
   identically everywhere (case-sensitive)?
6. Is every brush.* call spelled exactly as in the API list, with no invented methods?
7. Is `P5Brush`, `window`, or any other undeclared global absent from the whole function?
8. Is the total character count roughly between 300 and 2800 — not stripped down, not
   bloated with dozens of extra decorative calls?
Only once all eight are true, emit the single complete paint() function — no markdown
fences, no text before or after it.